Recorded in `FINDINGS.md` §12–13 and the REPORT's round-7 section, including one out-of-scope item I did **not** silently take: `xs.map(f)` is documented in SPEC.md § list and does not answer (pre-existing, a semantics decision about methods on a list *value*). Its error wording did change as a side effect of the receiver check — `Module 'xs' has no function 'map'` instead of the internal encoding `Unknown function 'xs_map'` — which is the better spelling and is noted in the report.
